209
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:17,000
Whatever they are, they are extremely powerful and they work behind the scenes in a realm that we can't typically see to steal worship from God and to destroy his good world.

210
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:24,000
And I know that this is a lot for many of us to grapple with.

211
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:31,000
In our post-enlightenment culture, we don't give too much thought to the things that we can't see or observe.

212
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:40,000
But I think we need to acknowledge that we are the minority throughout human history and even throughout geography in our current world.

213
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:47,000
And I think if we're really honest with ourselves, we actually don't understand near as much as we think we do.

214
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:50,000
I mean, gravity.

215
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:54,000
The theory of gravity.

216
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:56,000
We don't know what it is.

217
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:58,000
We can explain how it works.

218
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:02,000
We can kind of predict what's going to happen all of the time because it exists.

219
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:04,000
But what is it?

220
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:06,000
We don't know.

221
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:11,000
I love talking to some of my doctors and medical people in the room because they'll tell you that like,

222
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:18,000
when you hear a doctor talk about all of the things that are going on specifically with the brain or with the body or whatever,

223
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:22,000
they're like, we talk very confidently like we know what's going on.

224
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:28,000
We know a lot about a very small amount of things that are going on, right?

225
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:32,000
And this is just modern science that has developed over the last hundred years or so.

226
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:40,000
We do not have the answers that we think we have about existence and about depravity and about the brokenness of this world.

227
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:46,000
So I think if we can just take our enlightenment glasses off for a second and read the Bible on its terms,

228
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:53,000
we will have a much better understanding of what's actually going on in God's beautiful and broken world.

229
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:56,000
I love this quote from Glenn.

230
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:58,000
I can't pronounce your last name.

231
00:19:58,000 --> 00:20:00,000
Glenn, this is a great quote.

232
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:05,000
He says, "Pow, pow, pow."

233
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:06,000
All right.

234
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:09,000
I didn't major in English, so sorry.

235
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:12,000
The Bible is enchanted.

236
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:15,000
That is, the Bible is literally words with power.

237
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:18,000
It tells us how we've come to be enslaved.

238
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:29,000
It tells us of the coming of the word, Jesus, that can break the spell that lies over the human race.

239
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:31,000
Indeed, over the entire creation.

240
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:36,000
Unfortunately, many of our interactions with the Bible end up treating it as a very tame book.

241
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:47,000
We've worked pretty hard to make the Bible into a nice, tidy, even rationalistic collection of true, but very calm religious propositions.

242
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:49,000
We've missed the enchanted part.

243
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:53,000
And we've mostly just embraced the tame part.

244
00:20:53,000 --> 00:21:14,000
And I think as we continue to read the Scriptures and keep an eye out for all of this talk about the dark forces in the spiritual realm and all of the stuff that's going on in the Scriptures, we'll realize that there's a lot more going on and a lot more was accomplished by the blood of Jesus on the cross than we ever give it credit for.

245
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:16,000
That's true.

246
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:24,000
And although this is a lot to process, many of us probably who grew up in the church have some category for demonic forces, right?

247
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:26,000
You got something there.

248
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:34,000
Most of us kind of like we've got some underlying definition of that, that there are these demonic forces at work to destroy God's good world.

249
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:48,000
But I think at least in the spheres that I grew up in, we kind of shrunk their impact down into beings that tempt individuals to sin and give us flat tires when we're already having a bad day to try and make us cuss.

250
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:49,000
Right?

251
00:21:49,000 --> 00:22:01,000
This is kind of like my bringing up, even if you read the screw tape letters, which are awesome, it is like individual demon with individual Christian trying to make him stop being a Christian.

252
00:22:01,000 --> 00:22:09,000
But what Paul and the rest of the Bible seem to describe as something much bigger and much more powerful than that.

253
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:19,000
Not that that isn't true, but it's that it's broader and a wider scope that these are powerful beings who rule and reign in the heavenly realm.

254
00:22:19,000 --> 00:22:38,000
I would argue that they animate things like political empires, cultural identities, earthly identity markers, economic systems, even religious structures with lies aimed at destroying God's good world and dehumanizing image bearers all for the sake of their own worship.

255
00:22:38,000 --> 00:22:43,000
And it's important to make that emphasis on worship.

256
00:22:43,000 --> 00:22:44,000
That is their goal.

257
00:22:44,000 --> 00:22:54,000
They have rebelled against God who is worthy of all of our worship and they are doing everything they can to animate things on earth to draw us into worship things that are less than God.

258
00:22:54,000 --> 00:23:02,000
And when we are influenced by them, we are ultimately worshiping whatever the thing is that they are animating over God.

259
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:18,000
And we might even think we're worshiping money or we're worshiping sex or we're worshiping whatever the thing is that we worship, but we are worshiping demonic forces that are using that earthly thing to manipulate us over and above God's design for us in his good world.

260
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:25,000
And as sophisticated Westerners, we never acknowledge that what we're doing is idol worship.

261
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:30,000
But when we give our allegiance, hold on a second.

262
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:43,000
When we give our allegiance to political parties, cultural identities, the love of money, or even religious structures, we are worshiping idols.

263
00:23:43,000 --> 00:23:56,000
And the fruit of that is that we end up viewing other image bearers as enemies to be defeated rather than people to be loved.

264
00:23:56,000 --> 00:24:10,800
Because when we identify with some category that is less than image bearer of God, then we find allegiance with the people who look like us and agree with our ideas and embrace our things.

265
00:24:12,160 --> 00:24:22,460
And anybody who has an opinion that differs from our category of people that we have identified with, it's us versus them.

266
00:24:22,460 --> 00:24:24,340
And we need to win.

267
00:24:24,340 --> 00:24:29,020
And so we will justify doing some unchristian things in order to win an argument.

268
00:24:33,160 --> 00:24:49,080
And what Paul seems to be saying here is that the gospel is the manifold wisdom of God is so much more than saving individuals from their sins, but it is reconciling all things both on earth and in heaven to himself through the blood of Jesus.

269
00:24:52,280 --> 00:24:57,540
The best way that I can think to illustrate this reality is a Broadway stage.

270
00:24:57,540 --> 00:25:08,800
And it works biblically too, because when you read the book of Revelation, John has a revelation in the Greek apocalypse, right?

271
00:25:08,800 --> 00:25:11,480
It literally just means a pulling back of the curtain.

272
00:25:11,480 --> 00:25:16,940
What John is doing in Revelation is he's allowing us to see what is going on in the heavenly realms.

273
00:25:18,020 --> 00:25:27,220
And so what I would argue that Paul is saying here is that he's saying that all of creation is a cosmic playwright directed by God.

274
00:25:27,220 --> 00:25:29,640
God has created the world.

275
00:25:29,640 --> 00:25:32,020
He's created the stage, the set, the script.

276
00:25:32,020 --> 00:25:33,280
It's all God's.

277
00:25:33,280 --> 00:25:42,760
And he has given human actors on a visible stage the opportunity to rule and reign with him, to act out the play in accordance with his good design.

278
00:25:42,760 --> 00:25:47,640
The principalities and powers are like stagehands, lighting directors, sound techs.

279
00:25:47,660 --> 00:25:48,500
They're behind the scenes.

280
00:25:48,500 --> 00:25:51,360
You can't see them unless the curtain's pulled back.

281
00:25:51,360 --> 00:25:58,800
But again, all of this was intended to work together towards God's good design of a world that is flourishing.

282
00:25:58,800 --> 00:26:03,440
But humans have rejected God's script, and we've embraced our own versions of that script.

283
00:26:03,440 --> 00:26:10,000
Different actors have gathered together into different categories and different identities, and we are acting our own script out.

284
00:26:10,000 --> 00:26:15,780
And we have competing actors acting a different script out, and we are at war with one another on the stage.

285
00:26:16,100 --> 00:26:23,680
Meanwhile, behind the stage, the powers are animating the sinfulness of humanity with lies about creation, about God, and about other humans.

286
00:26:24,300 --> 00:26:36,300
They are manipulating the story for their own selfish decisions, and they break humanity into lesser identities, and they create rivalries and tension that lead to war, poverty, slavery, and all injustice.

287
00:26:36,300 --> 00:26:40,520
This is what has happened to God's good world, and oftentimes we don't think about it.

288
00:26:40,520 --> 00:26:41,360
We don't see it.

289
00:26:41,360 --> 00:26:42,020
It's out of sight.

290
00:26:42,020 --> 00:26:42,680
It's out of mind.

291
00:26:42,680 --> 00:26:45,040
Christianity is about me and what God did for me.

292
00:26:45,040 --> 00:26:46,300
It's so much bigger than that.

293
00:26:46,400 --> 00:27:05,980
And in the midst of this cosmic play where humanity is warring with one another, God steps in, and he partners with one specific group of actors called the nation of Israel, and he works with them, inviting them to work back towards his redemption of the good world.

294
00:27:07,600 --> 00:27:17,220
And they have some ups and some downs, but ultimately they fail, and they give themselves back over to the powers and principalities at work in the world.

295
00:27:19,020 --> 00:27:21,960
So Jesus leaves the director's chair.

296
00:27:21,960 --> 00:27:27,580
God incarnate, the word, became flesh, dwelling among us.

297
00:27:27,580 --> 00:27:34,260
Jesus stepped onto the stage, and the powers thought they smelt blood in the water.

298
00:27:34,260 --> 00:27:38,700
If they can just get Jesus to rebel with them.

299
00:27:38,700 --> 00:27:40,880
It's what Matthew 4 is all about.

300
00:27:40,880 --> 00:27:44,240
Jesus is baptized, the Father, the Son, the Holy Spirit.

301
00:27:44,240 --> 00:27:46,700
They declare, this is my Son in whom I am well pleased.

302
00:27:46,700 --> 00:27:55,940
All is going according to plan, and the Holy Spirit forces God out into the wilderness to wrestle with the Satan, a power and principality at work to try and get Jesus to rebel.

303
00:27:55,940 --> 00:27:57,380
The powers are like, all right, this is it.

304
00:27:57,380 --> 00:28:02,900
Our plan to steal God's worship from him for ourselves, it's all going according to our plan.

305
00:28:02,900 --> 00:28:06,160
If we can just get Jesus to rebel, which he does not.

306
00:28:06,160 --> 00:28:07,700
Okay, move on to next plan.

307
00:28:07,700 --> 00:28:09,140
Plan B, let's just kill him.

308
00:28:09,140 --> 00:28:12,000
If we can kill him, we win.

309
00:28:12,000 --> 00:28:14,260
God's vision of the world is over for good.

310
00:28:14,680 --> 00:28:17,360
And all the worship that is due him will be ours.

311
00:28:17,360 --> 00:28:20,140
At least that's what they thought.

312
00:28:20,140 --> 00:28:27,960
But this is the manifold wisdom of God.

313
00:28:27,960 --> 00:28:33,180
The thing that they thought would ultimately lead to their victory.

314
00:28:34,840 --> 00:28:43,660
Behind the scenes, behind the scenes, manipulating both the Pharisees and the Sadducees, who, again, are two very different groups of people that don't like each other.

315
00:28:43,660 --> 00:28:46,640
The powers got them to work together to try and kill Jesus.

316
00:28:46,640 --> 00:28:50,280
They couldn't do it on their own, so they went to a Roman government.

317
00:28:50,280 --> 00:28:59,400
Again, powers and principalities at work behind earthly governments and religious structures to try and kill Jesus and win the battle in the end.

318
00:28:59,460 --> 00:29:01,800
But this is the manifold wisdom of God.

319
00:29:01,800 --> 00:29:05,880
The thing that they thought would lead to their victory ultimately leads to their demise.

320
00:29:05,880 --> 00:29:11,600
Genesis chapter 3, they bruised his heel, but he crushed their head.

321
00:29:18,240 --> 00:29:23,480
The gospel is about so much more than forgiving you of your individual sins and sending you to heaven when you die.

322
00:29:23,480 --> 00:29:25,920
It is about that, but it is about so much more than that.

323
00:29:25,920 --> 00:29:27,280
First Corinthians chapter 2.

324
00:29:28,420 --> 00:29:34,900
We declare God's wisdom, a mystery that has been hidden and God destined for our glory before time began.

325
00:29:34,900 --> 00:29:41,600
None of the rulers of this age understood it, for if they had, they would not have crucified the Lord of our glory.

326
00:29:41,600 --> 00:29:45,440
This is the powers thinking they smelt blood in the water.

327
00:29:45,440 --> 00:29:47,740
If we kill Jesus, we win.

328
00:29:47,740 --> 00:29:52,120
And the thing that they thought led to their victory ultimately led to their defeat.

329
00:29:54,200 --> 00:30:04,220
Through the death, burial, resurrection, and ascension of Jesus, those of us who have placed our allegiance in him have been rescued from the domain of darkness and brought into the kingdom of life.

330
00:30:04,220 --> 00:30:16,260
The multi-ethnic and unified church now shows the rulers and authorities the manifold wisdom of God's redemption plan in Christ that had been seated before the foundation of the world.

331
00:30:20,420 --> 00:30:22,460
All right, note takers, you can flip your bulletin over.

332
00:30:22,460 --> 00:30:26,040
I think we're making a pretty good time.

333
00:30:26,040 --> 00:30:41,540
All right, what I did here is I took two different images that Tim Mackey, the great biblical illustrator of our day, made, and I tried to make them into one.

334
00:30:41,540 --> 00:30:45,380
And by me trying to make them into one, I mean that April Crosby made them into one.

335
00:30:45,460 --> 00:30:45,840
Thank you.

336
00:30:45,840 --> 00:30:52,040
Some are hands, some are feet, some are Canva illustrators, all right?

337
00:30:52,040 --> 00:30:54,060
Can we throw that up on the screen, Dave?

338
00:30:54,060 --> 00:31:02,400
And so this is, to me, a visualization of what Paul has done here from Ephesians chapter 1 to Ephesians chapter 3,

339
00:31:02,400 --> 00:31:08,060
showing us the whole implications of the gospel, that heaven and earth were overlapping.

340
00:31:08,060 --> 00:31:16,080
And in rebellion, both of humanity and of the powers and principalities, we now have our little sweat of the brow emoji.

341
00:31:16,080 --> 00:31:21,100
And when Dr. Richter was here, she talked about the curse being the sweat on the brow.

342
00:31:21,100 --> 00:31:24,300
It's more than just work is hard in a sinful fallen world.

343
00:31:24,300 --> 00:31:27,960
It's that we are afraid that we are not going to have enough for us and for our people.

344
00:31:29,180 --> 00:31:37,320
And so that forces us into different groups, different tribes and ethnicities and languages and identity markers.

345
00:31:37,320 --> 00:31:44,520
And that's represented by all of the different colors that we kind of push ourselves into smaller categories.

346
00:31:44,520 --> 00:31:50,140
We're no longer just image bearers that were made to flourish together, but we are different categories of image bearers.

347
00:31:50,140 --> 00:31:55,580
And this is what Paul talks about when he says there's no more male or female, slave or free, Jew or Gentile.

348
00:31:55,580 --> 00:32:02,500
These are all categories that we have lumped ourselves into and we fight against one another.

349
00:32:02,500 --> 00:32:05,860
In the patriarchy of the first century, it was male versus female.

350
00:32:05,860 --> 00:32:09,260
And there was domination and there was injustice all around.

351
00:32:09,260 --> 00:32:12,540
And slaves and masters, injustice all around.

352
00:32:12,600 --> 00:32:21,080
And we have different categories of people and we treat people who are in our category, in our sphere, better than people who don't look like us or talk like us or act like us.

353
00:32:21,080 --> 00:32:22,460
We are at war with one another.

354
00:32:22,460 --> 00:32:35,800
And I would argue that the powers and principalities are at work behind those earthly categories, animating them for their own selfish desires, resulting in rivalry, war, poverty and injustice.

355
00:32:37,800 --> 00:32:49,620
And what Jesus does on the cross and the burial and the resurrection, and this is why the language about being raised above the heavenly realms and seated with God in Christ is so important.

356
00:32:49,620 --> 00:32:56,200
Because what Jesus does is he gathers for himself a group of people from every language, tribe, nation and tongue.

357
00:32:56,200 --> 00:33:00,040
And notice here, this is back to last week, notice the color stay, right?

358
00:33:00,040 --> 00:33:02,740
We're not asking us to all become one culture.

359
00:33:02,740 --> 00:33:06,080
We get to keep our earthly cultural identity markers.

360
00:33:06,080 --> 00:33:09,200
We get to keep our ethnicity, our language, our culture, our food.

361
00:33:09,200 --> 00:33:10,240
We get to keep all of that.

362
00:33:10,240 --> 00:33:11,320
It's beautiful and good.

363
00:33:11,320 --> 00:33:16,380
But we lay it down as the primary identity marker of our lives.

364
00:33:16,380 --> 00:33:32,860
And we pick up the primary identity marker of Jesus, making us a member of one unified church, a new family of God that has been raised above the powers and principalities in the air, seated with Christ in the heavenly places, making us the new working model of new creation on earth.

365
00:33:32,860 --> 00:33:37,560
We no longer have to be afraid of other categories of people that are going to take from us.

366
00:33:37,560 --> 00:33:46,180
We can actually work towards the life and flourishing of all people created in the image of God for his glory and for the good of our neighbor.

367
00:33:47,640 --> 00:33:51,720
It's this fear and insecurity that has been taken advantage of by the powers.

368
00:33:51,720 --> 00:33:58,520
We're all competing for limited resources and we do whatever it takes to win at all costs.

369
00:33:58,520 --> 00:34:02,420
And the trajectory of this is every kind of injustice under the sun.

370
00:34:03,200 --> 00:34:13,120
But now through Christ, we can be reborn and given a new primary identity where there's no more slave or free, Jew or Gentile, male or female, Republican or Democrat.

371
00:34:13,120 --> 00:34:21,900
We all are one in Christ, raised with him and seated with him above the influence of the powers and principalities of the air.

372
00:34:21,900 --> 00:34:25,340
We get to live as children of God who aren't afraid anymore.

373
00:34:25,340 --> 00:34:29,060
It's not that life isn't hard.

374
00:34:29,060 --> 00:34:32,860
It's not that we won't not have enough from time to time.

375
00:34:32,860 --> 00:34:35,500
But this is where Jesus steps in and he says, look at the birds of the air.

376
00:34:35,500 --> 00:34:37,700
Look at the lilies of the field.

377
00:34:37,700 --> 00:34:40,220
Do not be afraid.

378
00:34:43,520 --> 00:34:45,980
Everything I have is yours.

379
00:34:45,980 --> 00:34:49,280
I own a cattle on a thousand hills.

380
00:34:49,280 --> 00:34:50,680
It's all mine.

381
00:34:50,680 --> 00:34:52,640
You don't have to be afraid.

382
00:34:52,640 --> 00:34:56,380
You don't have to break into subcategories and war with one another for limited resources.

383
00:34:56,380 --> 00:35:00,360
You can live with your hands open and trust that I will provide for you.

384
00:35:00,360 --> 00:35:10,920
And if I'm being honest, I think many in the American church have lost the plot.

385
00:35:13,360 --> 00:35:19,000
I'm not sure that we're revealing God's manifold wisdom to the rulers and authorities

386
00:35:19,000 --> 00:35:22,500
as much as we are sitting in the palm of their hands.

387
00:35:22,500 --> 00:35:28,360
Disunified, segregated, and fighting political wars with earthly weapons

388
00:35:28,360 --> 00:35:31,280
rather than a kingdom war with spiritual weapons.

389
00:35:31,280 --> 00:35:40,840
There's this strange verse in Matthew that I've always not understood

390
00:35:40,840 --> 00:35:45,440
where Jesus says that, you know, there's this Antichrist that are going to come.

391
00:35:45,440 --> 00:35:47,140
They're going to do everything they can to deceive.

392
00:35:47,140 --> 00:35:50,600
And he says, if possible, even the elect.

393
00:35:50,600 --> 00:35:55,780
And I look at this chart

394
00:35:55,780 --> 00:36:03,340
and I see the powers and principalities doing everything they can to deceive the nations,

395
00:36:03,900 --> 00:36:07,420
to deceive the political parties, to deceive the empires,

396
00:36:07,420 --> 00:36:10,540
to deceive the whatever your temporary identity marker is.

397
00:36:10,540 --> 00:36:17,500
And if possible, they will still continue to try and deceive us.

398
00:36:17,500 --> 00:36:25,520
To stop living like we're in Christ, raised above the powers and principalities,

399
00:36:25,520 --> 00:36:29,320
seated with Christ, unified with people from every language, tribe, nation, and tongue.

400
00:36:29,760 --> 00:36:34,640
They will do everything they can to get us to not live like the working model of new creation on earth.

401
00:36:34,640 --> 00:36:41,040
And I think in many ways, we've kind of allowed them to do that to us.

402
00:36:41,040 --> 00:36:43,200
We need repentance.

403
00:36:43,200 --> 00:36:49,520
We need to recapture the mystery of the power of God to redeem and reconcile us

404
00:36:49,520 --> 00:36:54,020
into one new, unified family, working together for justice, life,

405
00:36:54,020 --> 00:36:57,220
and flourishing for God's good world gone wrong.

406
00:36:57,220 --> 00:37:01,740
I know this is a lot of information.

407
00:37:01,740 --> 00:37:04,240
This is the longest I've ever taken to prep a sermon.

408
00:37:04,240 --> 00:37:08,800
I probably could have used another 20 hours, but that's not how time works.

409
00:37:08,800 --> 00:37:12,520
So you're getting the underdeveloped version.

410
00:37:12,520 --> 00:37:14,380
I know there's a lot of information.

411
00:37:15,480 --> 00:37:19,340
I'd love for you to take this chart home and just sit with it and think about,

412
00:37:19,340 --> 00:37:26,860
is my primary identity marker in Christ,

413
00:37:26,860 --> 00:37:30,380
raised above the powers and principalities of this era

414
00:37:30,380 --> 00:37:32,500
and seated with him in the heavenly places?

415
00:37:32,500 --> 00:37:37,400
Is my primary identity with the church?

416
00:37:37,400 --> 00:37:41,160
Do I have more in common with my brothers and sisters

417
00:37:41,160 --> 00:37:45,760
who have bowed the knee to Jesus who live in Africa or Asia or Palestine

418
00:37:45,760 --> 00:37:48,640
or Israel or Russia or Ukraine?

419
00:37:48,640 --> 00:37:50,740
Or do I have more in common with the dude

420
00:37:50,740 --> 00:37:52,980
who likes the same sports team as I down the road

421
00:37:52,980 --> 00:37:54,320
and who votes the way that I vote?

422
00:37:54,320 --> 00:37:58,920
What is our primary identity marker?

423
00:37:58,920 --> 00:38:01,320
Where is our primary allegiance?

424
00:38:01,320 --> 00:38:03,660
Because if we keep giving our allegiance to things

425
00:38:03,660 --> 00:38:05,520
that are lesser than being in Christ,

426
00:38:05,520 --> 00:38:07,660
raised above the powers and principalities

427
00:38:07,660 --> 00:38:09,380
and seated with him in the heavenly places,

428
00:38:09,380 --> 00:38:12,800
adopted into one new multi-ethnic family of God,

429
00:38:12,800 --> 00:38:15,600
if we keep giving our allegiances to less than that,

430
00:38:15,600 --> 00:38:18,440
then we will fight earthly wars with earthly weapons

431
00:38:18,440 --> 00:38:25,880
rather than kingdom ones with spiritual weapons.

432
00:38:28,820 --> 00:38:31,040
Is it possible we've accepted Christ

433
00:38:31,040 --> 00:38:33,200
but given ourselves back over to the deception

434
00:38:33,200 --> 00:38:36,300
of the rulers and authorities?

435
00:38:36,300 --> 00:38:44,620
All right.

436
00:38:44,620 --> 00:38:47,460
That was the biggest chunk, the hardest chunk.

437
00:38:47,460 --> 00:38:48,980
We're gonna move on.

438
00:38:48,980 --> 00:38:50,200
Is that all right?

439
00:38:50,200 --> 00:38:52,040
All right.

440
00:38:52,840 --> 00:38:55,480
Paul moves on in chapter 12, verse 12

441
00:38:55,480 --> 00:38:58,940
to talk about a perspective on persecution.

442
00:38:58,940 --> 00:39:02,060
He says,

443
00:39:02,060 --> 00:39:05,080
in him and through faith in him,

444
00:39:05,080 --> 00:39:08,360
we may approach God with freedom and with confidence.

445
00:39:08,360 --> 00:39:10,700
I ask you therefore not to be discouraged

446
00:39:10,700 --> 00:39:13,040
because of my sufferings for you,

447
00:39:13,040 --> 00:39:15,140
which are your glory.

448
00:39:15,140 --> 00:39:18,100
What are Paul's sufferings here in verse 13?

449
00:39:18,100 --> 00:39:20,360
He told us in verse one,

450
00:39:21,280 --> 00:39:25,060
Paul, a prisoner for the sake of Christ Jesus.

451
00:39:25,060 --> 00:39:26,720
Paul is in jail

452
00:39:26,720 --> 00:39:30,200
because of this message

453
00:39:30,200 --> 00:39:33,540
that Christ foiled the plans

454
00:39:33,540 --> 00:39:35,540
of the powers and principalities of the air.

455
00:39:35,540 --> 00:39:38,700
That he came back to life,

456
00:39:38,700 --> 00:39:41,800
that he rose from the dead,

457
00:39:41,800 --> 00:39:43,200
that he ascended into heaven

458
00:39:43,200 --> 00:39:45,460
and that he is ruling and reigning.

459
00:39:45,460 --> 00:39:49,480
And I don't know about you,

460
00:39:49,560 --> 00:39:51,100
but if my king,

461
00:39:51,100 --> 00:39:53,660
the one who I gave my entire life to,

462
00:39:53,660 --> 00:39:55,940
to preach this message,

463
00:39:55,940 --> 00:39:57,920
was truly ruling and reigning

464
00:39:57,920 --> 00:40:00,420
and I found myself in a Roman prison,

465
00:40:00,420 --> 00:40:03,200
I might be thinking,

466
00:40:03,200 --> 00:40:05,920
are you ruling and reigning?

467
00:40:05,920 --> 00:40:09,280
Because I'm in prison

468
00:40:09,280 --> 00:40:13,400
